76 edits. Suite still green: 69 passed, 1 skipped, 0 failed.

COPY. Five patterns accounted for nearly all of it:

- "Research shows mature believers grow through modeling and practice"
  cited no research. It is now stated as our own observation, which is what
  it always was. This was also a breach of the project's own rule that
  nothing gets asserted without a source.
- Six "not X, it's Y" negative parallelisms on Next Steps alone. Removed
  four, kept the two carrying real weight.
- Promotional adjectives stated as fact, concentrated on Ministries:
  authentic, vibrant, transformative, "we're passionate about". Worst case
  was "hope and healing are here" inside the GriefShare description, where
  marketing language does the most harm.
- Around forty em dashes in running prose, several twice in one sentence.
  Converted to colons, commas and full stops. Label uses left alone
  ("Jesus — Savior", "Sundays — 9:00 & 10:30 AM").
- British spellings on the College page: programme x3, specialisation,
  specialised, recognisable.

Left deliberately untouched: the mission and values statements on What We
Believe, and the two College paragraphs that read as quoted from LPU's own
deck. Institutional language is not ours to rewrite.

TUITION FIGURES. The Ministries page published "$12K per year" and
"50-70% less than average private college". LIFE-PACIFIC-YAKIMA.md line 143
records that the cost figures are still unknown, and line 56 states the
cost-comparison framing "is dead - do not revive it". The page had revived
it. Published dollar figures for a degree program are a different order of
risk from loose copy, so both are replaced with facts drawn from our own
College page, keeping the three-stat layout intact: "Mon-Thu / mornings on
campus" and "AA-DMin / degrees you can earn here".

The $2,000 site fee stated on the College page is still unconfirmed against
the same checklist item.

FACTUAL CONTRADICTION. Home said the service runs about 70 minutes, Next
Steps said 75. Harmonised to 75 pending confirmation - one of them is wrong
and I could not determine which.

Still unresolved and NOT guessed at: Cheree is "Discipleship Director" on
the team page and "Discipleship Pastor" on Next Steps.

PHOTOS.md rewritten. It claimed there was not one photograph on the site
apart from the hero, which stopped being true when the twelve team
portraits landed. Now records the real state (13 in place, 12 outstanding)
with ratios and delivery sizes per slot.

